ed the role  for a short amount of time  unfortunately for brolin roger moore  decided to come back to the franchise  after all  killing any dreams of an american bond  maybe one day  having opened in 1935 pinewood studios  has been with bond since the very  beginning  but during their 60 years of filming  there the franchise's cast and crew have  endured their fair share of disasters  in 1984 the stage on which most of the  bond films were shot  tragically burned to the ground it took  a full year to rebuild and it was  eventually renamed as the albert r  broccoli 007 stage in honor of the  legendary producer  unfortunately the double 07 stage burned  down again in 2006  at the time the double 07 stage was  actually being used for a bond movie and  the blaze ended up destroying the fake  venice used in casino royale  luckily the filmmakers had just finished  shooting no one was hurt and there  weren't any dangerous pyrotechnics or  flammable objects around to make things  worse  even so it took around 90 minutes to get  the fire under control  by 2007 the double 07 stage was open  again  newly enlarged and now it's one of the  biggest sound stages in europe  james bond has always pulled out the  stops when it comes to theme songs  among the legendary artists who have  written for the franchise are shirley  bassey paul mccartney madonna gladys  knight carly simon  tom jones and ace of base yes indeed the  90s swedish pop group ace of base was  actually hired to ride a bond theme  where pierce brosnan's bond debut  goldeneye sadly the head honchos at our  wrist at records the label that  represented the band thought goldeneye  was going to be a flop  and they didn't want their primo band  associated with failure so artista  pulled ace of base from the project and  the james bond folks went with  tina turner instead however the swedish  band did rename their track the juvenile  and if you're interested you can still  hear the double-oh-seven song that could  have been  a number of other famous artists have  written bond themes over the years too  only to follow the final hurdle blondie  were locked in to pen the title track to  for your eyes only for a while  johnny cash wrote his own version of  thunderball and pulp almost did the  theme for tomorrow never dies  even radiohead almost got in on the bond  action writing a title track for spectre  that sadly was rejected by producers  because it was in their opinion too dark  for the movie  after sean connery left the franchise  the producers were adamant that they  should find the perfect replacement for  him but nobody could have guessed it  would be george lazenby  the australian car mechanic who fell  into male modeling according to lazenby  he had never acted in his life but when  he got the info about auditions during  the threesome the man decided he would  work as hard as he could to win the  producers over  over the next four months they made him  jump through a number of poops including  a screen test with a wrestler who lays  and be accidentally knocked out  then in a genuinely shocking move the  producer sent him a sex worker to make  sure he wasn't gay  this never happened to the other fella  given that he allegedly ended up  sleeping with almost every girl on set  however it seems like lazenby passed  that particularly disturbing test  in fact lazenby actually did well with  his first bond film on her majesty's  secret service and was even offered a  one million dollar contract to star in  six more movies  but his agent at the time told him to  turn it down according to his agent the  bond age was over and people were more  into gritty films like easy rider  so lazenby left bond behind and was  eternally blackballed for being a nobody  that turned down the biggest franchise  around  roger moore was a man of many talents  not only did he play double07 but he has  also written about the iconic spy too  in his book bond on bond more gives  ample insight into the world o