lights but he  couldn't get out of his tv contract for  remington steel  fortunately the producers came back  around to brosnan when he was  conflict-free  but while he brought in new energy to  the franchise brosnan never felt happy  with his performances bond  as the man himself put it i felt i was  caught in a time warp between roger  moore and sean connery the violence was  never real the brute force of the man  was never palpable  it was quite tame and the  characterization didn't have a follow  through of reality it was surface  but then that might have had to do with  my own insecurities and playing him as  well  as the latest actor to play james bond  daniel craig has plenty of mixed  feelings about the iconic role  he takes the film seriously and loves  the work of course but also once called  the role a drag and has occasionally  insisted he wants nothing less than to  never play the role again  more recently however he has walked back  those comments calling his gig as the  super spy the best job in the world  so what's up with the mixed emotions  well maybe craig feels so conflicted  because bond is his complete opposite as  the actor once told time  out i was aware of what was needed to be  bond but it still goes against  everything i believe in  you've met me a couple of times i'm not  very cool but  bond has to be cool he goes on to say  and that often feels awkward for him  though you'd never guess that daniel  craig thinks he's kind of a dork it's  easy to understand the pressure of  playing the smoothest character in film  history  still if the popular reception to his  bond is anything to go by  craig really doesn't have anything to  worry about  the name's bond james bond  check out one of our newest videos right  here plus even more looper videos about  your favorite movies are coming soon  subscribe to our youtube channel and hit  the bell so you don't miss a single one

